== now reboot ==
[a16-bt-arm] Any of the DT rows ([1] [2] [3] [4]) now loads the Bluetooth test DTB, so the
[a16-bt-arm] next boot gets it whether or not the menu is touched.  After it comes up:

    bash /home/jc/a16-payload/a16-bt-setup.sh status

[a16-bt-arm] Expect, in that output:
    serdev client: PRESENT, stub rails: 6 of 6
    then either a controller under /sys/class/bluetooth (hci0 -- Bluetooth is up), or the
    qca firmware lines in the kernel log naming the file it wanted.  Both are real datums;
    'MISSING /dev/ttyHS1' is expected and harmless -- serdev means there is no tty.

[a16-bt-arm] To go back to the stock DTB:  sudo bash /home/jc/a16-payload/a16-bt-arm.sh revert
[a16-bt-arm] If the machine will not come up at all: pick the [0] row (ACPI, no devicetree
[a16-bt-arm] line, so it is immune to this), then run the revert above.  From Windows, the
[a16-bt-arm] ESP's a16boot\glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dtb.a16stock copied back over
[a16-bt-arm] glymur-asus-zenbook-a16-ux3607oa.dtb also restores it.
